# Copy to .env.local and adjust if needed. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Must point at an address the backend's Kestrel process actually binds to
# (see src/WalletLedger.Api/Properties/launchSettings.json -> applicationUrl).
# On WSL2, that means http://localhost:5037, not the WSL gateway/adapter IP:
# the API process (dotnet.exe) binds to Windows' loopback interface only, and
# the browser making the request also runs on the Windows side, so localhost
# is what actually resolves for both. Pointing this at the WSL gateway IP
# (e.g. 172.21.128.1) looks like a plausible WSL2-networking fix but isn't -
# nothing listens there, so every request fails at the network level and the
# app surfaces it as a generic "Something went wrong" with no HTTP status.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5037
